// EMPTY ARCADE — FILTER DISCO — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// EMPTY ARCADE as French-touch filter house — a game alternate of title, on the desk; the title
// screen itself always plays title.js. Peter: "some groovy new remixes for the ... title music".
// The empty arcade's neon flickering back on: Stardust / Cassius / Modjo-era filter disco.
// 
// THE HOOK is title.js's lead note for note, at its own 3-3-2 sixteenths, which at 124 is a
// two-bar chopped disco loop on the title's chords coloured for house, a chord a half bar:
//   | Am9  Fmaj9 | Cmaj9  G9sus4 (F/G) |   — the last sixteenth's A4 pushes the next Am9.
// Played by one FRPP-6 funk guitar (frppFunkRhythm) as chord stabs with the tune on top, voiced
// one note per string, Alternate strum (down-strokes on the eighths, ups 4 dB under). Its 6 → 8
// is two down-strokes round an air stroke, which a per-strike Alternate cannot say, so the hook
// sits on two lanes of the one guitar (same preset, same pan); muted chucks (frppFunkMuted) fill
// the hand's free sixteenths under the same parity; the Rhodes (rmndTineEP, phaser) doubles the
// stabs. The loop, bass and strings pump on the Banger French House LOOP_PUMP.
// THE BREAKDOWN sings the tune at half speed (a chord a bar) — within 10 % of the title's own 56.
// THE FILTER is master Spot FX: a resonant low-pass at 420 for the intro (its first beat
// flickering on), opening to 4500 over the 8-bar build and slamming open at 13; closing 14k→650
// over 29–32, opening 650→5000 over 33–44 and slamming open at 45; closing to 420 over the outro
// so the loop (5–68) wraps into the build.
// 
//   1–4    POWER ON: the loop alone behind a closed low-pass, the neon flickering on; kick at 3
//   5–12   BUILD: master low-pass 420→4500 over 8 bars; bass 5, chucks, hats 7, clap 9, riser + roll 11–12
//   13–28  DROP ONE: the filter slams open; loop + chucks pumping, octave bass, 909 kit; strings + shaker at 21
//   29–36  BREAKDOWN: drums out, filter closing 29–32; the tune at half speed (the nocturne's own pace) on the vocoder, Rhodes, strings, twinkle; clean guitar + held bass from 33
//   37–44  BUILD TWO: the loop returns under the still-opening filter; kick 37, hats 39, clap 41, riser + roll 43–44
//   45–60  FINAL DROP: slam open; the talk box on the hook, strings, shaker; bright guitar an octave up from 53
//   61–68  OUTRO: master low-pass closing to 420 over 8 bars; parts peel away back to loop + bass + kick → bar 5
// 
// Sounds: FRPP-6 funk rhythm ×2 lanes, funk muted, funk bright (octave line), clean electric,
// string section, plucked synth bass (+ a sine under the roots); RMND-7 Rhodes; JMJR-4 Robot
// Chant as a vocoder (ooh) and a talk box (wah), 30 ms glide; TNGR-2 celesta; 909 kit. No CRLS-1.
// Levelled to −24 LUFS (the menu line) by the trailing master gain (-5.8 dB).
// 68 bars at 124, 132 s; the loop 5–68 is 124 s.
// Written by work/local/_title-remix-filter-disco.mjs through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs, which
// self-checks chord tones, semitone clashes, one note per string, strum parity and the loop wrap.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
